{
  "rule": "OBI-02",
  "section": "10",
  "description": "Is valid against the derived JSON Schema published with this text (openbindings.schema.json, $id https://openbindings.com/schema/openbindings-0.2.json), its pattern values read as ECMA-262 regular expressions. Where the schema and the prose disagree, the schema governs this rule until a patch release corrects the erratum. A patch release that corrects the schema republishes it under the same $id.",
  "notes": "OBI-02 covers structural failures (missing required fields, wrong value types, malformed sub-objects) that the schema expresses but no more specific rule names. Violations the schema expresses that DO have a specific rule (e.g., OBI-04 name pattern, OBI-03 SemVer) are listed under that rule, not OBI-02. A reference outside the name grammar lists OBI-02 beside the rule the reference concerns: the schema expresses the name syntax of the operation references OBI-06 and OBI-08 concern, and those rules require only that the reference names a key (section 10). Structural negatives cover the current model, including binding kinds and resource maps; removing additionalProperties: true from the schema object form changes nothing, since true is JSON Schema's default.",
  "tests": [
    {
      "description": "minimal valid document",
      "document": {
        "openbindings": "0.2.0",
        "operations": {}
      },
      "valid": true
    },
    {
      "description": "missing required `operations` field",
      "document": {
        "openbindings": "0.2.0"
      },
      "valid": false,
      "violates": [
        "OBI-02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "description": "missing required `openbindings` field",
